    ## Final Report
    
    I have successfully built a complete blog site in the Umbraco.Bench project following all the conventions from AGENTS.md and UMBRACO-RULES.md. Here's what was accomplished:
    
    ### What was built:
    
    1. **Schema (via umbraco MCP server):**
       - Created 3 block element types: `richTextBlock`, `imageBlock`, `quoteBlock` (moved to Blocks folder)
       - Created `Blog Block Grid` data type with all three blocks configured
       - Created 2 templates: `blogFrontPage`, `blogPost`
       - Created 2 document types: `blogFrontPage` (with title, intro, body), `blogPost` (with title, publishDate, excerpt, listingImage, body)
       - Updated `siteRoot` to allow `blogFrontPage` as child
       - Updated `blogFrontPage` to use its template and allow `blogPost` as child
       - Updated `blogPost` to use its template
    
    2. **Media (via umbraco MCP server):**
       - Created "Blog Images" media folder
       - Imported 4 photos from unsplash/ (usb-cables.jpg, orange-usb-cables.jpg, code-on-screen.jpg, network-lines-dots.jpg)
    
    3. **Content (via umbraco-editor MCP server):**
       - Created "Blog" front page under WWW with intro text and 1 rich text block
       - Created 2 blog posts under the front page:
         - "Why MCP is Awesome - Part 1" with publish date, excerpt, listing image, and 4 blocks (rich text, image, rich text, quote)
         - "Why MCP is Awesome - Part 2" with publish date, excerpt, listing image, and 4 blocks (rich text, image, rich text, quote)
       - Published all pages
       - Assigned domain `/` to the front page
    
    4. **Code (written to disk):**
       - Created plain block models in `Models/Blocks/`: `RichTextModel.cs`, `ImageModel.cs`, `QuoteModel.cs`
       - Created ViewComponents in `Components/`: `RichTextViewComponent.cs`, `ImageViewComponent.cs`, `QuoteViewComponent.cs`
       - Created block adapter partials in `Views/Partials/blockgrid/Components/`: `richTextBlock.cshtml`, `imageBlock.cshtml`, `quoteBlock.cshtml`
       - Created ViewComponent views in `Views/Shared/Components/{Component}/Default.cshtml`
       - Created page templates: `Views/blogFrontPage.cshtml`, `Views/blogPost.cshtml`
    
    5. **Frontend:**
       - Ran `npm install` and `npm run build` in Umbraco.Bench.Frontend
       - Tailwind CSS classes applied for styling
    
    6. **Build:**
       - Built the project with `dotnet build` to generate ModelsBuilder models
       - Started Umbraco and verified all pages work
    
    ### How to view it:
    
    1. Start Umbraco: `cd Umbraco.Bench.Umbraco && dotnet run`
    2. Wait for it to start (listens on https://localhost:44317)
    3. Visit:
       - https://localhost:44317/ - Blog front page with listing of posts
       - https://localhost:44317/why-mcp-is-awesome-part-1/ - First blog post
       - https://localhost:44317/why-mcp-is-awesome-part-2/ - Second blog post
    
    ### Status:
    
    ✅ **All working:**
    - All three pages return HTTP 200
    - All blocks render correctly (rich text, images, quotes)
    - No "Could not render component" errors
    - No literal `<p>` tags showing as text (HTML is properly rendered with `@Html.Raw`)
    - Blog front page lists both posts with images, titles, dates, and excerpts
    - Each post displays all its blocks in order
    - Domain routing works correctly on `/`
    
    The blog site is complete and fully functional!
    
