    ## Report: Blog Site Implementation
    
    I have successfully built a complete blog site in the Umbraco.Bench project using the MCP servers. Here's what was accomplished:
    
    ---
    
    ### ✅ What Was Built
    
    **1. Schema (via umbraco MCP server):**
    - Created 3 element types (blocks): `richTextBlock`, `imageBlock`, `quoteBlock` - all moved to Blocks folder
    - Created `Blog Block Grid` data type with all 3 blocks configured
    - Created 2 document types: `blogFrontPage` and `blogPost` in Pages folder
    - Created 2 templates: `blogFrontPage` and `blogPost`
    - Updated document types with templates and allowed children (siteRoot → blogFrontPage → blogPost)
    
    **2. Media (via umbraco MCP server):**
    - Created "Blog Images" media folder
    - Imported 4 photos from unsplash/ (USB cables, orange USB cables, code on screen, network lines)
    
    **3. Content (via umbraco-editor MCP server):**
    - Created "Blog" front page under WWW with title, intro, and 1 rich text block
    - Created 2 blog posts under the front page, each with:
      - Title, publish date, excerpt, listing image
      - 4+ blocks: rich text, image, more rich text, quote
    - Published all pages
    - Set domain `/` on the front page
    
    **4. Code Generation & Views:**
    - Built project to generate ModelsBuilder models
    - Created plain block models in `Models/Blocks/`
    - Created 3 ViewComponents in `Components/`
    - Created component views with Tailwind styling
    - Created blockgrid adapter partials
    - Created page templates with full HTML structure
    - Built frontend assets with `npm run build`
    
    **5. Testing:**
    - All 3 pages return HTTP 200
    - All blocks render correctly (rich text as HTML, images with captions, quotes with attribution)
    - No literal `<p>` tags showing as text
    - No "Could not render component" errors
    
    ---
    
    ### 📋 How to View
    
    1. Start Umbraco: `cd Umbraco.Bench.Umbraco && dotnet run`
    2. Wait for it to start (https://localhost:44317)
